## 1. Role and Product Definition

You are a **senior desktop architect, Rust/Tauri engineer, Python data-platform engineer, and M&V/statistical-modeling expert**. Build a **production-grade, offline, single-user Windows desktop application**.

| Layer | Decision |
|---|---|
| Platform | **Windows 10 22H2 and Windows 11, x64** (system WebView2) |
| Shell | **Tauri 2** (Rust) |
| Frontend | React 19 + TypeScript (strict) + Vite + Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn/ui (Radix) |
| Engine | **Python 3.11+** sidecar, frozen with PyInstaller **onedir** |
| IPC | **JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdin/stdout** (NDJSON). **No HTTP, no localhost ports.** |
| Storage | SQLite via SQLAlchemy 2.x + Alembic, with zero-fail boot |
| Packaging | Tauri **NSIS** installer, one `EnergyBaseline.exe` launcher, `.lnk` with custom `.ico` |

**Product flow [M]:** ingest time-series data → column setup → **Variable Selection Gate** → **Test Configuration** → profile, diagnose, and mine data → identify drivers → build an **independent baseline per TARGET** → compare a broad portfolio (including neural networks) → show a **Top-5 per target with explicit representation** → **user selects and locks one** → unlock **Prediction & Monitoring** (file / external SQL / manual) → deviation vs the locked baseline, drift status, interactive dashboard. **AUTO is available on every user-selectable setting, with a documented resolution log.**

