## 11. Multi-Target Independence [M]

- **MT-1** One or more TARGETs, each with an **independent end-to-end pipeline** (VSG state, preprocessing, leakage rules, feature selection, portfolio, HPO, Top-5, lock).
- **MT-2 Leakage rules (per target):**
  - other TARGETs are never predictors;
  - predictors **not available at prediction time** are excluded in forward mode;
  - a predictor with |r| ≥ 0.99 is flagged “suspected leakage” and **AUTO-excluded only if** it shares the target’s declared unit family or an algebraic identity is detected;
  - otherwise it is kept with a warning, and the user may override. All of this is logged.
- **MT-3** Targets run sequentially or in parallel (capped by cores) with per-target progress and a global cancel. **The merged AUTO log is sorted by target, not by completion order.**
- **MT-4** Per-target seed = `hash(global_seed, target_id)`.
- **MT-5 [S]** **Conditional diagnostics:** regime labels (F4) are used to produce conditional correlation matrices, conditional coverage, and conditional CV(RMSE); labels are **never** model inputs (leakage).

