## 17. Modeling and Validation

### 17.1 Portfolio
- **Mandatory [M] baseline set:** mean baseline; degree-day regression; MLR; Ridge; Lasso; Elastic Net; piecewise/change-point (1P–5P aligned with ASHRAE 14, verify the exact variant list); TOWT; Random Forest; ExtraTrees; Gradient Boosting; XGBoost; LightGBM; SVR (RBF); MLP; **at least one sequence NN (LSTM, GRU, or TCN)**.
- **[S]:** polynomial deg-2, GAM (B-splines), Bayesian ridge, quantile regression, Gaussian Process (**with an AUTO size cap and a sparse/subsample strategy, documented**), 1D-CNN, CNN-LSTM, autoencoder regressor.
- **[O]:** CatBoost, N-BEATS, TFT, PatchTST, Informer. Anything not shipped is listed as “not implemented”.
- **Constraints [M]:** expected-sign and monotonicity settings (TCP-4) are applied where the model family supports them; otherwise they are checked post-hoc and reported.
- **NN gate [M]:** an NN is rejected if it does not beat the best classical model's CV(RMSE) by the margin (AUTO default 5 %), or if its parameter count exceeds the observation count. The reason is recorded.
- **Ensemble [M]:** a blend is created only if it improves out-of-fold CV(RMSE) by > 3 % (AUTO-logged). **Blend weights are learned by constrained NNLS on inner-fold OOF predictions and evaluated on outer folds** (never fit and scored on the same OOF). If the data cannot support learned weights, use an equal-weight heuristic and label it as such.
- **Baseline artifact [M]:** every locked model exports a safe artifact (ONNX/skops/JSON coefficients where possible; pickle only with SHA-256 verification and a user warning). A **model card** is produced (intended use, training window, features, assumptions, calibration summary, known limitations).

### 17.2 Validation design [M]
- **VAL-1** Blocked K-fold for histories < 2 years (contiguous folds, seasonal coverage checked and logged); forward-chaining otherwise.
- **VAL-2** **Purge gap ≥ max(1 day, 1 sampling step, max lag, max rolling-window length).**
- **VAL-3** Nested tuning: HPO runs inside each training fold. **Scaling, imputation and feature selection (Boruta/RFE/Lasso/MI/Granger-based screening) are fit inside training folds only**, as part of one pipeline object. Only variables in the **Candidate Pool** (PIPE-2) are eligible; `force_include` variables bypass selection (VSG-1).
- **VAL-4** HPO: Optuna (TPE default; random and CMA-ES selectable; seeded sampler). **CMA-ES requires `optuna.samplers.CmaEsSampler`; verify it exists in the installed Optuna version (some 2026 builds removed it — if absent, use the `cmaes` package or skip with a logged deviation)**. Trials scale with data size under AUTO (3–8 for very small, 15–25 for 200–5,000 rows, 5–10 for very large) with a per-model time budget.
- **VAL-5** **Final untouched holdout** (the most recent block; AUTO-enabled when n is sufficient). The locked model's holdout metrics are reported separately to expose selection bias (winner's curse).
- **VAL-6** Feature constraints: collinearity pruning at |r| ≥ 0.95, then iterative VIF (threshold 10, or 5 when n < 100); `k_max = min(p, n/20)`. Pruning never removes a `force_include` variable silently; conflicts are shown.
- **VAL-7 Metric definitions (state formulas and sign convention in the report):** `CV(RMSE) = sqrt(Σ(y−ŷ)²/n) / ȳ × 100`; `NMBE = Σ(y−ŷ) / (n·ȳ) × 100`; guard |ȳ| ≈ 0 (metrics become “undefined” with a flag); sMAPE guarded the same way. Primary metrics are out-of-fold and **without** a DoF correction. For parametric models also report Guideline-14-style DoF-adjusted in-sample values, labeled separately.

