## 19. Uncertainty Quantification [M]

- **UQ-1 [M]** Default is **conformal prediction** via **MAPIE v1**: `SplitConformalRegressor`, `CrossConformalRegressor`, `JackknifeAfterBootstrapRegressor`, `ConformalizedQuantileRegressor`, and the **`TimeSeriesRegressor`** class (methods `"enbpi"` or `"aci"`) for time-series baselines. **Verify the exact class names in the installed MAPIE v1.x before use.**
- **UQ-2 [M]** Coverage is selectable (80/90/95/99 %); the default follows the global confidence level (TCP-1).
- **UQ-3 [M] Honesty:** exchangeability is violated by autocorrelated series, so coverage is **approximate**. Report rolling empirical coverage and never claim a distribution-free guarantee for time series.
- **UQ-4 [M] Calibration report:** empirical vs nominal coverage (reliability diagram), mean interval width, Winkler/interval score, **conditional coverage by regime** (load level, season, F4 clusters), and the **T12 tests** (Kupiec, Christoffersen). PIT histograms **only** for models with predictive distributions (GP, Bayesian ridge, MC-dropout).
- **UQ-5 [M]** The residual-quantile (or block-bootstrap) method is retained as a labeled fallback. Bayesian posterior and MC-dropout/deep-ensemble intervals may be shown alongside, clearly labeled, and only if calibration shows they are competitive.

