## 29. Final Constraints (Restated) [M]

- Implement a **working system**, not a plan or mock-up, **milestone by milestone** (§3), starting with **M-1 (Bootstrap & Skeleton)**.
- **Never hallucinate metrics, test results or library APIs.** Compute and verify. Every custom test has an R reference.
- **Never silently delete or alter data.** Log everything, including every test-driven action and every outlier treatment.
- **Desktop, offline, Windows, Tauri 2 + Python sidecar. No Electron, no browser, no localhost server.**
- **SQLite-first**; external SQL is an optional Prediction input.
- **The user chooses variables (VSG) and test policy (TCP) before any test runs.** Integrity rules cannot be disabled.
- **AUTO everywhere**, with documented reasoning and a recorded `AUTO` vs `USER_OVERRIDE` mode. Fast Mode and Full Mode both produce a valid result.
- **Comprehensive test catalog, confidence intervals everywhere, exhaustive EDA/data mining, and a fully narrated, chart-rich report.**
- **Top-5 with explicit representations** before locking. **Multi-target independence** end to end. **Conformal UQ** by default.
- **All UI, reports, logs and docs in English.** The UI is i18n-ready.
- Document every assumption and every deviation. No LLM in the report path.